; Leg CH -- the host SENDS.  The Victor RECEIVES on the KEEP_ICP build.
;
; NO TRANSFER HAS EVER BEEN RUN WITH THE PARSER BUILD.  That is the whole
; content of this leg.  Edit 14 widened what main() compiles -- it moved a
; mis-nested #endif in ckcmai.c, which is the one edit in this port that is
; not a no-op elsewhere -- so the parser binary is not the binary any
; throughput figure in this project was measured on.  dofast() is inside the
; widened region and is guarded out on purpose (SS8 item 14), because it
; sets wslotr = RBSIZ/MAXSP = 2 and would have opened the window to two,
; unmeasured, on a port with no flow control and a 105-byte ring margin.
;
; So this leg asks one question: did the wire protocol move?  A byte-exact
; md5 with rxlost=0 rxfull=0 says no.
;
; PRECONDITION, and it is a trap rather than an inconvenience.  CKICP.EXE on
; the image must be the 9 August rebuild (435,154 bytes, md5 f5456cae).  The
; copies staged on 8 August predate upstream edits 16 and 17.  Without edit
; 17, chk3() computes the CRC in long through two long[16] tables, which at
; 38400 with block check 3 pinned rxpeak at 4,095 of 4,096 and lost 556-649
; bytes on three legs of four (SS16af).  Run this against a stale binary and
; you reproduce that ring defect and read it as "the parser build breaks
; transfers" -- a wrong conclusion that would look thoroughly convincing,
; because rxfull would be non-zero and the resends real.
;
; The Victor side is RXEA.KSC, already on the image and already CRLF:
; set line /dev/seriala, set speed 38400, set receive timeout 20, receive,
; statistics, exit.  It takes the filename from this end's F packet, so the
; Victor writes RCVCH.DAT -- a name that is not on the image, because SET
; FILE COLLISION is BACKUP and BACKUP cannot work on FAT.

set speed 38400
set receive timeout 20
set parity none
set prefixing cautious
set block 3
log packets s16aiCH.pkt
send rcvch.dat
statistics
